TEXT -144 224 Left 2 ;The vntol parameter is rather high\n(to achieve fast simulation)
TEXT -48 -16 Left 2 ;Sync of generator at 2s (t_sync=2000ms)\nAVR on at 2.5s ( t_enable_avr=2.5s  t_enablev_avr=2s)\nFix outher torque at 2s (t_stop_nreg=2010m t_start_fixm=2000m)
TEXT -336 0 Left 2 ;If you plot Q you can see that the synchronous machine\nconsumes more and more Q if the P output gets higher \nand higher. This is although the voltage is regulated by\nAVR at 115kV. If the vsoll value is set to a higher value\n(e.g. 116kV)  the Q consumtion can be (partially) \ncompensated by the higher magnetic field voltage
TEXT -48 24 Left 2 ;vsoll is set to 116kV to let the \ngenerator consume less Q at full load\nAT vsoll = 117kV the generator\nwill even deliver Q to the voltage source\nAnother possiblity is a constant\nQ controller (example as sgen_constant_Q_controller.asc)\nin Synchronous_machine_examples directory
TEXT 32 200 Left 2 ;Q = 3*Us*Up/omega * [Us/Up-cos(delta)] OR\nQ = 1.5*(usy*isx-usx*isy)\nP = 1.5*(usx*isx+uxy*isy) \n-> Q=max if delta=90 Grad \n-> Q=min if delta=0 Grad\nAlso regulating of Q through Us/Up\nUp>Us overexitation - Q (Voltage higher)\nUp<Us underexitation +Q (Voltage lower)
TEXT -272 264 Left 2 ;Starting time of ,TRAN card\nis set to 10ms because of \nlarge spike at startup of the\nPV element
TEXT -272 200 Left 2 !.param fn1=50 omega_n={2*pi*fn1}
TEXT -336 -56 Left 2 ;NOTE: If Gen-PV-element paramter err0=1 (full volatage at startup) is present \nthere is a voltage spike at startup -> set tenable=30us for the P,Q,Phasemeter device
